window.JH_MANUAL_PUBLIC = {"first":3,"last":14,"pages":["Customer guide / Welcome to Jolly Helmet! A self-service station that cleans and dries your motorcycle helmet while you wait. Meet the machines There are three Jolly Helmet stations. Each one has a touch screen, a coin slot and a door. Pick the one that fits what your helmet needs. Station What it does Box 1 Cleaner Removes odor. UV light plus a fine mist of alcohol, scented liquid, or both. Box 2 Dryer Dries a wet helmet with warm air, then cools it down before you take it out. Box 3 Cleaner + Dryer One station, two modes. Choose CLEANING or DRYING on the first screen. Tip / Paalala: Pwede mong gamitin ang Box 1 at Box 2 nang magkasunod: linis muna, tapos tuyo. Which machine is free? Look for the QR sticker on the machines. Scan it with your phone camera. A page opens that shows Box 1, Box 2 and Box 3 as FREE, IN USE (with about how many minutes are left) or OUT OF ORDER. You do not need an app or a password. The button at the top changes the language between English and Filipino. When a machine is running your cycle you may also tap Add your name on its card and type a nickname (12 letters at most). Everybody who opens the page sees it, so use a nickname, not your full name. It disappears by itself when your cycle ends.","/ The customer status page: which machine is free (phone) Tip / Paalala: I-scan ang QR sticker para makita kung aling makina ang libre. Pindutin ang \"Filipino\" sa itaas ng page. Before you start You need: your helmet and coins. The machine counts coins by value: a one-peso coin counts as 1. How the touch screen works / Rating grid: tap a box 1-10, then CONFIRM / Number pad: type the minutes and seconds, then OK Big words (yellow) tell you what to do next: OPEN, PLACE, CLOSE, TAKE. Buttons are the dark boxes with white words. Tap them once. The screen blinks briefly now and then. This is normal, it refreshes itself.","Never put your hand in while the machine runs. If you open the door, the machine pauses by itself.","Box 1 - Cleaner / 1. Tap anywhere to START / 2. Welcome Wake the machine. Tap anywhere on the screen. For a moment it says \"Please Wait\" while it checks its alcohol and scented liquid. Tap to START on the welcome screen. If the screen says OUT OF ORDER, the station needs refilling or service. Please tell the staff. Rate it and choose the mist / 3. ODOR O\u0027 METER / 4. CLEANING MODE Rate the smell. Tap 1 (MINT, fresh) to 10 (STINKY), then CONFIRM. The worse the smell, the more time we suggest. Choose the mist. BALANCED uses both liquids, MORE ALCOHOL is stronger against germs, MORE SCENTED leaves a fresher scent.","Pick the time and pay / 5. ALLOCATE CLEAN TIME / 6. INSERT THE REQUIRED COIN Allocate time. The pad shows the time we suggest for your rating. Type a different time if you like, then tap OK. The shortest time and the longest time are shown if you go outside them. Insert the coins. The screen counts up: coins inserted / coins required. When it is enough, the machine moves on by itself. Extra coins beyond the price give no extra time and are not refunded. Tap CANCEL before paying if you change your mind. Load your helmet / 7. OPEN / 8. PLACE / 9. CLOSE OPEN the door when the screen asks. PLACE your helmet inside, opening facing the front, then step back. CLOSE the door. The machine checks that the door is shut and the helmet is inside, then starts. If you see HELMET NO DETECTED, the machine did not see your helmet. Open the door and place it again.","While it cleans / 10. Cleaning... time left / CANCEL asks first The big green number is the time left. The bar fills as it goes. The small grey line shows what is on: the mist, the UV light. To stop early tap CANCEL, then CONFIRM. Coins are not refunded. RESUME keeps cleaning. If the door is opened during a run, everything pauses (SAFETY PAUSE). Close the door and it continues where it stopped. All done / 11. TAKE your helmet / 13. FREE TIME? OPEN the door and TAKE your helmet. Close the door again. Rate it again on the same 1-10 grid, then CONFIRM. Free retry. Not happy yet? The machine may offer a short FREE TIME (2 minutes). Tap YES to run once more, or NO. It is offered once per visit. The screen thanks you and returns to the start.","Box 2 - Dryer / DRY O\u0027 METER / ALLOCATE HEATING TIME Tap anywhere, then Tap to START (same as Box 1). Rate how wet it is: 1 = DRY ... 10 = WET, then CONFIRM. Allocate heating time on the number pad, then OK. Insert the coins shown on the screen. OPEN, PLACE, CLOSE the door, same as Box 1. Heating and cooling / 6. Heating... / 7. Cooling Down... Heating. Warm air dries the helmet and UV light freshens it. You can CANCEL, but coins are not refunded. Cooling down. A fan runs alone so the helmet is not hot to wear. The door stays locked until it ends. OPEN the door, TAKE your helmet, CLOSE the door. Rate it again, then use the free retry if you want one. If you cancel while heating, the machine still cools the helmet down first, for your safety.","Box 3 - Cleaner + Dryer / SELECT MODE / CLEANING unavailable Tap anywhere, then Tap to START. SELECT MODE. Tap CLEANING or DRYING. If CLEANING is grey and says UNAVAILABLE, the cleaning liquids are being refilled or are low. DRYING still works. CLEANING mode Same steps as Box 1: rate the odor, choose the mist, pick the time, pay, load the helmet. At the end you rate two things: how dry it is, then how it smells. The heater runs only in the last minute, together with the UV light. DRYING mode / Drying... / Cooling Down... Rate how wet the helmet is (DRY O\u0027 METER), then CONFIRM. Allocate drying time on the number pad. Pay, then OPEN, PLACE, CLOSE. Drying uses warm air and UV light. After it, the machine cools down for about a minute with nothing running.","OPEN, TAKE, CLOSE, rate again and use the free retry if offered. A free retry after cleaning is another cleaning; after drying it is another drying.","Prices and time Box 1 and Box 3 (cleaning): 15 coins = 5 minutes. Rating Suggested time Coins 1 - 5 5 minutes 15 6 - 7 10 minutes 30 8 - 9 15 minutes 45 10 20 minutes 60 Longest session: 30 minutes (90 coins). Box 2 (drying): 10 coins = 3 minutes. Rating Suggested time Coins (about) 1 - 3 3 minutes 10 4 - 6 5 minutes 17 7 - 8 8 minutes 27 9 - 10 10 minutes 34 These are the starting prices. The admin can change them, so always check the INSERT THE REQUIRED COIN screen for the exact amount.","Special screens and safety Special screens / Door opened during a run / Station needs service You see What it means / what to do SAFETY PAUSE The door was opened. Close it and the run continues. HELMET NO DETECTED No helmet seen. Open the door and place it again. OUT OF ORDER The station cannot work now. Use another station and tell the staff. CLEANING UNAVAILABLE Cleaning liquids are low. Use DRYING or come back later. MAINTENANCE A technician is working on the station. Safety first Helmets only. Do not put bags, gloves, liquids or anything else inside. Keep your hands out while the machine runs. Hot air and UV light are used. UV light is strong. Never look into the chamber while it is on. The door must be closed. Do not force the door. It is locked on purpose while the machine runs. To stop, use CANCEL on the screen. If the screen does not answer, use the safety slide (see \"If the door will not open\"). Remove your helmet\u0027s accessories (camera, speaker, visor tint film) if they are not heat-safe. Children should use the machine with an adult. In an emergency, tap CANCEL, then CONFIRM. The machine stops and the door unlocks (on the dryers after a short cool-down). If your helmet is stuck after a power cut or a fault, do not pull on the door. Slide the safety lock down (lower left of the enclosure door): the door unlocks at once. Then tell the staff. If the door will not open The door is locked on purpose while a machine runs. If the screen does not answer, the power is off, or the lock is broken, you can always open the door yourself with the safety slide. Look at the lower left corner of the enclosure door. The safety slide is there.","Slide it down. The door unlocks at once, with or without power. Open the door and take your helmet out. Tell the staff afterwards. / The safety slide: lower left of the enclosure door. Slide it down to unlock (drawing) If the machine was running, opening the door stops it (SAFETY PAUSE) and switches the UV light and the heat off. The UV light is strong: do not look into the chamber until it is off. The helmet may be warm. Questions Question Answer The screen went white. Wait a moment, it restarts itself. If it stays white, tell the staff. I inserted a coin but nothing changed. Insert the coin again slowly. Tell the staff if the count does not move. Can I get a refund? Coins are not refunded after the run has started or been cancelled. The time is too long / too short. On the number pad, type the time you want before tapping OK. Why was I offered a free retry? Because the helmet may need one more round. It is offered once per visit. Which station should I use? Smelly: Box 1 or Box 3 CLEANING. Wet: Box 2 or Box 3 DRYING. The door will not open. Wait until the run ends, or tap CANCEL. If the screen does not answer or the power is off, slide the safety lock down (lower left of the enclosure door)."],"toc":[{"t":"Customer guide","l":1,"p":3},{"t":"Meet the machines","l":2,"p":3},{"t":"Which machine is free?","l":3,"p":3},{"t":"Before you start","l":2,"p":4},{"t":"How the touch screen works","l":3,"p":4},{"t":"Box 1 - Cleaner","l":2,"p":6},{"t":"Rate it and choose the mist","l":3,"p":6},{"t":"Pick the time and pay","l":3,"p":7},{"t":"Load your helmet","l":3,"p":7},{"t":"While it cleans","l":3,"p":8},{"t":"All done","l":3,"p":8},{"t":"Box 2 - Dryer","l":2,"p":9},{"t":"Heating and cooling","l":3,"p":9},{"t":"Box 3 - Cleaner + Dryer","l":2,"p":10},{"t":"CLEANING mode","l":3,"p":10},{"t":"DRYING mode","l":3,"p":10},{"t":"Prices and time","l":2,"p":12},{"t":"Special screens and safety","l":2,"p":13},{"t":"Special screens","l":3,"p":13},{"t":"Safety first","l":3,"p":13},{"t":"If the door will not open","l":3,"p":13},{"t":"Questions","l":3,"p":14}]};
